; (शत is used in the
 singular with a plural noun of any gender; शतं नराः; शतं गावः;
 or शतं गृहाणि, in which case it is treated as a numeral adjective;
 but sometimes in dual and plural also; द्वे शते, दश शतानि &c. It
 is also used with a noun in the genitive; गवां शतम्, वर्षाणां शतम्
 ‘a century of cows, years’ &c. At the end of comp., it may remain unchanged;
 भव भर्ता शरच्छतम् or may be changed into शती; as in आर्यासप्तशती
 a work of Govardhanācārya.).
